    <bpmn:process id="W_W1178" name="W1178. Predictive Analytics Model Development, Deployment &amp; Monitoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Business need for predictive capability; or annual analytics roadmap planning; or pilot success triggering production deployment
Frequency: ~4–6 new model development projects per year; continuous monitoring of production models
Volume: 3–5 production models in operation at any time; serving 200 stores and 4 DCs
Owner: Data Scientist / BI Manager
Participants: Data Scientist, BI Manager, Business Domain Owner (Category Manager, VP Supply Chain, CHRO), Data Engineer, IT Operations
Source: workflow W1178 — Predictive Analytics Model Development, Deployment &amp; Monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1178_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1178_Lane1" name="BI Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1178_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1178_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1178_Lane2" name="Data Scientist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1178_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1178_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1178_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1178_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1178_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1178_Lane3" name="Data Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1178_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1178_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1178_Start5" name="Business need for predictive capability; or annual analytics roadmap planning; or pilot…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1178_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1178_Task6" name="Use case identification &amp; prioritization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Use case identification &amp; prioritization: Annual planning + ad-hoc: (a) BI Manager and business domain owners identify predictive analytics use cases; (b) score each use case on: business impact (revenue, cost, risk), data availability and quality, technical feasibility, and implementation effort; (c) prioritize top 4–6 use cases for annual roadmap; (d) CIO approves roadmap and budget; (e) quick wins (high impact, low effort) scheduled for H1
Responsible (R): BI Manager / Business Domain Owner
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1178_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1178_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1178_Task7" name="Data exploration &amp; preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Data exploration &amp; preparation: For each approved use case: (a) Data Scientist explores available data: historical sales (POS), inventory movements, customer transactions, vendor performance, weather, economic indicators; (b) assess data quality per W1177 governance standards; (c) build feature engineering pipeline: derive predictive variables (lagged sales, rolling averages, seasonality indicators, store demographic features); (d) prepare training data set with appropriate time splits; (e) document data sources, transformations, and assumptions
Responsible (R): Data Scientist / Data Engineer
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1178_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1178_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1178_Task8" name="Model development &amp; validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Model development &amp; validation: (a) Data Scientist trains multiple model types: time series (ARIMA, Prophet), regression (XGBoost, LightGBM), neural networks (for complex patterns); (b) cross-validate using walk-forward validation for time series; (c) compare model performance vs. baseline (current W31 forecast, random baseline, naive seasonal baseline); (d) select best model based on: accuracy (MAPE, RMSE), interpretability, computational cost, robustness; (e) document model architecture, hyperparameters, and performance metrics; (f) Business Domain Owner reviews model logic for business plausibility
Responsible (R): Data Scientist
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 2–6 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1178_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1178_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1178_Task9" name="Pilot deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Pilot deployment: (a) deploy model in pilot scope: 1–2 product categories for demand sensing, or 1 region for churn prediction; (b) run model alongside existing process for 4–8 weeks; (c) compare model predictions to actual outcomes; (d) measure business impact: forecast accuracy improvement, churn reduction, inventory risk identification lead time; (e) iterate on model based on pilot findings; (f) Business Domain Owner approves for production based on pilot results
Responsible (R): Data Scientist / Data Engineer / BI Manager
Accountable (A): Business Domain Owner
Duration: 4–8 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1178_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1178_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1178_Task10" name="Production deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Production deployment: (a) Data Engineer integrates model into production data pipeline: scheduled batch scoring (nightly for demand sensing, weekly for churn, monthly for inventory risk); (b) IT Operations deploys model infrastructure (cloud compute, API endpoints); (c) integrate model outputs into existing workflows: demand forecast feed to W31 S&amp;OP, churn scores to W660 retention program, inventory risk scores to W587 obsolescence review; (d) build monitoring dashboard showing model predictions, accuracy, and drift metrics
Responsible (R): Data Engineer / IT Operations
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1178_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1178_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1178_Task11" name="Ongoing model monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Ongoing model monitoring: Continuous monitoring: (a) Prediction accuracy: track MAPE/RMSE weekly; alert if accuracy degrades &gt; 20% from baseline; (b) Data drift: monitor input feature distributions for shifts (e.g., sales pattern change after new competitor enters market); (c) Concept drift: monitor if relationship between features and target changes (e.g., economic downturn changes price sensitivity); (d) Business KPI impact: track if model-driven decisions actually improve business outcomes; (e) monthly model health report to BI Manager
Responsible (R): Data Scientist / System
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1178_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1178_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1178_Task12" name="Model retraining &amp; retirement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Model retraining &amp; retirement: (a) quarterly: retrain models with latest data to incorporate new patterns; (b) if retrained model significantly outperforms production model: promote to production; (c) if model consistently underperforms baseline: retire model and revert to existing process; (d) document model version history and performance trajectory
Responsible (R): Data Scientist
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1178_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1178_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1178_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1178_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1178_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-327 (ensure controlled execution — Advanced Analytics (PA-28.3).) | - operational: Data Scientist / BI Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Data Scientist / BI Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1178_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1178_Annotation14" targetRef="W1178_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1178_Flow16" sourceRef="W1178_Start5" targetRef="W1178_Task6" />
