    <bpmn:process id="W_W1215" name="W1215. Customer Segmentation &amp; Basket Analysis for Category Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly category management review cycle; or triggered by Category Manager request for new product introduction decision; or annual customer segmentation refresh
Frequency: Quarterly analysis deliverables; annual full segmentation refresh
Volume: ~600,000 loyalty members + ~5,200 trade accounts segmented; 33.6M annual transactions analyzed for basket patterns
Owner: BI Analyst / Category Manager
Participants: BI Analyst, Category Manager, Loyalty Program Manager, VP Merchandising, Ecommerce Manager
Source: workflow W1215 — Customer Segmentation &amp; Basket Analysis for Category Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1215_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1215_Lane1" name="BI Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1215_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1215_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1215_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1215_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1215_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1215_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1215_Lane2" name="Loyalty Program Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1215_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1215_Lane3" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1215_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1215_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1215_Start5" name="Quarterly category management review cycle; or triggered by Category Manager request for…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1215_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1215_Task6" name="Data preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Data preparation (quarterly): BI Analyst extracts transaction data from data warehouse: (a) all POS and ecommerce transactions for the quarter, (b) linked customer identifiers (loyalty card, trade account, guest), (c) item-level detail with category hierarchy, (d) transaction metadata (store, date/time, channel, payment method), (e) customer master attributes (segment, tenure, location, tier)
Responsible (R): BI Analyst
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1215_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1215_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1215_Task7" name="Customer segmentation refresh">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Customer segmentation refresh (annual): BI Analyst refreshes customer segmentation model using RFM (Recency, Frequency, Monetary) analysis + category affinity: (a) calculate RFM scores for each customer, (b) cluster customers into segments: (i) Trade Loyalists (high frequency, high value, trade account), (ii) Weekend Warriors (moderate frequency, DIY categories, weekends), (iii) Project Planners (low frequency, high value per trip, project-oriented purchases), (iv) Convenience Shoppers (high frequency, low value, proximity-driven), (v) Digital Natives (ecommerce-primary, younger demographic), (vi) Lapsed Customers (no purchase in 90+ days); (c) validate segments with Category Managers for business plausibility; (d) publish segment assignments to CRM for campaign targeting
Responsible (R): BI Analyst / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 weeks (annual)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1215_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1215_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1215_Task8" name="Basket analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Basket analysis (quarterly): BI Analyst conducts market basket analysis on quarterly transaction data: (a) Affinity analysis: identify SKU pairs/groups with high co-occurrence (lift &gt; 1.5) — e.g., tiles + tile adhesive + grout, aircon + copper tubing + electrical wire; (b) Category adjacency: which categories are bought together in same trip?; (c) Sequential purchasing: items bought in repeat visits within 30 days (project phased purchasing); (d) Channel comparison: in-store vs. ecommerce basket size, composition, and cross-sell patterns; (e) Trade vs. DIY: basket profile comparison between trade accounts and walk-in customers
Responsible (R): BI Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1215_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1215_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1215_Task9" name="Segment profitability analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Segment profitability analysis (quarterly): BI Analyst calculates contribution by segment: (a) revenue and gross margin by customer segment, (b) average basket size and margin by segment, (c) cost-to-serve by segment (trade accounts require credit management per W24; ecommerce requires fulfillment cost; walk-in requires store staffing), (d) lifetime value estimation for each segment
Responsible (R): BI Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1215_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1215_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1215_Task10" name="Category management insights delivery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Category management insights delivery: BI Analyst presents findings to Category Managers: (a) Cross-sell opportunities: &quot;Customers who bought X also bought Y&quot; for display pairing, bundle creation per W1, and POS suggestive selling per W748; (b) SKU rationalization: identify SKUs with zero cross-sell value and low standalone sales — candidates for discontinuation; (c) Assortment gaps: customer segments purchasing categories outside BuildRight (identified from loyalty survey data) — opportunity for new product introduction; (d) Planogram insights: high-affinity categories should be co-located in store layout per W86; (e) Promotional targeting: segment-specific promotion recommendations (e.g., Trade Loyalists respond to bulk discounts; Weekend Warriors respond to bundle deals)
Responsible (R): BI Analyst / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 hours per category</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1215_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1215_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1215_Task11" name="Loyalty program personalization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Loyalty program personalization: Loyalty Program Manager uses segmentation to: (a) configure segment-specific earning rules per W496 (e.g., double points on paint category for Weekend Warriors), (b) create targeted campaign lists per W300 (e.g., &quot;Project Planner&quot; segment receives project completion reminder emails), (c) personalize in-app product recommendations based on segment and basket affinity
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1215_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1215_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1215_Task12" name="Category Manager documents decisions and actions taken based on analysis…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Category Manager documents decisions and actions taken based on analysis; tracks impact on subsequent quarter&#x27;s metrics (did cross-sell rate improve? did targeted promotions lift revenue?)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1215_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1215_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1215_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1215_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1215_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-327 (ensure controlled execution — Advanced Analytics (PA-28.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: BI Analyst / Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1215_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1215_Annotation14" targetRef="W1215_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
