    <bpmn:process id="W_W1251" name="W1251. Category Space Productivity Analytics &amp; Planogram Performance Measurement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — monthly category space productivity report; quarterly planogram compliance audit; ad-hoc triggered by category margin decline or planogram refresh request
Frequency: Monthly analytics; quarterly planogram compliance measurement; ad-hoc for new planogram validation
Volume: 35,000 active SKUs across 200 stores × 12 product categories; quarterly planogram audit for ~50 high-priority planograms
Owner: BI Analyst (Space &amp; Category Analytics)
Participants: Category Manager, Merchandising Planner, VP Store Operations, VP Merchandising
Source: workflow W1251 — Category Space Productivity Analytics &amp; Planogram Performance Measurement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1251_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1251_Lane1" name="BI Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1251_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1251_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1251_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1251_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1251_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1251_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1251_Start3" name="Scheduled — monthly category space productivity report; quarterly planogram compliance…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1251_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1251_Task4" name="Monthly category space productivity report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly category space productivity report: BI Analyst generates monthly report per category: (a) sales per sqm by category (using planogram fixture dimensions from space planning module); (b) gross margin per sqm by category; (c) GMROI (Gross Margin Return on Inventory Investment) per category; (d) inventory turns per category; (e) compare category productivity to national average and regional benchmarks; (f) flag categories where sales per sqm declined &gt; 5% month-over-month
Responsible (R): BI Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1251_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1251_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1251_Task5" name="Planogram compliance measurement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Planogram compliance measurement: Using planogram audit data from store visits (W86) and digital planogram compliance tools: (a) measure compliance rate — % of stores with correct planogram execution by category; (b) correlate compliance rate with sales performance — do high-compliance stores outperform low-compliance stores? (c) identify planograms with &lt; 80% compliance rate for corrective action; (d) report compliance by region — provincial stores typically have lower compliance than Metro Manila stores
Responsible (R): BI Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1251_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1251_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1251_Task6" name="Planogram sales lift validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Planogram sales lift validation: After planogram refresh (new planogram deployed): (a) measure 4-week and 8-week sales performance vs. pre-planogram baseline; (b) isolate planogram effect from promotional and seasonal effects; (c) calculate incremental sales per sqm from planogram change; (d) compute ROI of planogram investment (labor cost for reset vs. incremental margin); (e) validate or refute planogram hypothesis — share results with Category Manager
Responsible (R): BI Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 4 hours per planogram validation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1251_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1251_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1251_Task7" name="Underperforming space identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Underperforming space identification: Quarterly analysis to identify space reallocation opportunities: (a) rank all categories by sales per sqm; (b) identify categories where space allocation exceeds productivity contribution (e.g., 14% of space but 6% of sales); (c) identify high-productivity categories constrained by insufficient space; (d) model space reallocation scenarios — what would happen if 50 sqm moved from Garden to Power Tools?; (e) present recommendations to VP Merchandising for annual planogram rebalancing
Responsible (R): BI Analyst / Merchandising Planner
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1251_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1251_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1251_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1251_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1251_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-327 (ensure controlled execution — Advanced Analytics (PA-28.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: BI Analyst (Space &amp; Category Analytics)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
