    <bpmn:process id="W_W1252" name="W1252. Supply Chain Predictive Analytics, Demand Sensing &amp; Early Warning System" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — weekly demand sensing refresh; monthly model retraining; ad-hoc triggered by supply chain disruption alert or forecast accuracy degradation
Frequency: Weekly demand sensing update; monthly model performance review; quarterly model recalibration
Volume: 35,000 active SKUs across ~205 locations (200 stores + 4 DCs); weekly demand signal processing for all A-class and B-class SKUs (~17,500 SKUs)
Owner: Data Scientist / Supply Chain Analyst
Participants: Demand Planner, Category Manager, Import Coordinator, Logistics Planner, VP Supply Chain
Source: workflow W1252 — Supply Chain Predictive Analytics, Demand Sensing &amp; Early Warning System</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1252_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1252_Lane1" name="Data Scientist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1252_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1252_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1252_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1252_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1252_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1252_Lane2" name="Demand Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1252_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1252_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1252_Start4" name="Scheduled — weekly demand sensing refresh; monthly model retraining; ad-hoc triggered by…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1252_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1252_Task5" name="Weekly demand sensing refresh">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly demand sensing refresh: Data Scientist runs weekly demand sensing pipeline: (a) ingest external data feeds: PAGASA weather forecast, DOLE construction permit releases, cement/steel commodity price indices, social media trend signals for home improvement topics; (b) ML model generates adjusted demand forecast for next 12 weeks by SKU-location; (c) compare model forecast to current statistical forecast (W31) — flag SKUs where demand sensing forecast deviates &gt; 15%; (d) generate demand shift alerts: (i) emerging demand spike (construction activity uptick in a region), (ii) demand collapse (typhoon approaching — demand drops pre-landfall then spikes for emergency supplies), (iii) commodity price-driven substitution (steel price increase drives shift from rebar to alternative framing)
Responsible (R): Data Scientist
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1252_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1252_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1252_Task6" name="Alert triage &amp; action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Alert triage &amp; action: Demand Planner reviews demand sensing alerts: (a) validate top 20 alerts against market intelligence — are they real signals or noise?; (b) for validated demand spikes: check current on-hand, in-transit, and open PO coverage — is there sufficient stock to capture the demand?; (c) for validated demand collapses: review open import POs — should any be deferred or cancelled to avoid overstock?; (d) generate recommended actions: expedite PO, allocate safety stock increase, adjust replenishment parameters per W312; (e) escalate to Import Coordinator for PO action on import items
Responsible (R): Demand Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1252_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1252_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1252_Task7" name="Monthly model performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly model performance review: Data Scientist evaluates predictive model accuracy: (a) calculate MAPE (Mean Absolute Percentage Error) for demand sensing forecast vs. actual sales for past 4 weeks; (b) compare demand sensing MAPE to traditional forecast MAPE — is the ML model adding value?; (c) analyze false positive rate — how many alerts were validated vs. rejected?; (d) identify SKUs or locations where model performs poorly — feature engineering or data quality issues; (e) document model performance in monthly MLOps report
Responsible (R): Data Scientist
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1252_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1252_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1252_Task8" name="Quarterly model recalibration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly model recalibration: Retrain and recalibrate ML models: (a) update training data with latest 12 months of actual sales; (b) evaluate new external data sources (e.g., satellite imagery for construction activity, Google Trends data for DIY interest); (c) tune hyperparameters for improved accuracy; (d) A/B test recalibrated model vs. current model for 2 weeks; (e) deploy updated model if accuracy improvement &gt; 5% MAPE reduction
Responsible (R): Data Scientist
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 16 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1252_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1252_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1252_Task9" name="Early warning escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Early warning escalation: For critical supply chain disruptions (typhoon forecast, port congestion, political instability in import sourcing countries): (a) generate emergency demand impact assessment for all affected locations; (b) model stock-out risk for critical SKUs (cement, plywood, emergency supplies); (c) recommend pre-positioning actions — move inventory from low-risk DCs to high-risk regions; (d) brief VP Supply Chain and COO on recommended response
Responsible (R): Data Scientist / Demand Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4 hours per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1252_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1252_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1252_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1252_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1252_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-327 (ensure controlled execution — Advanced Analytics (PA-28.3).) | - operational: Data Scientist / Supply Chain Analyst review and approval gate
Owner: Data Scientist / Supply Chain Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
