    <bpmn:process id="W_W1398" name="W1398. Customer Churn Prediction Model, At-Risk Account Identification &amp; Proactive Retention Campaign" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — monthly model scoring run; quarterly model performance review
Frequency: Monthly scoring (all active accounts); quarterly model review and retraining
Volume: ~5,400 trade and corporate accounts scored monthly; ~600K loyalty members scored quarterly
Owner: Senior Data Scientist
Participants: Senior Data Scientist, BI Manager, Credit Manager, Loyalty Manager, Head of Trade / Account Management
Source: workflow W1398 — Customer Churn Prediction Model, At-Risk Account Identification &amp; Proactive Retention Campaign</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1398_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1398_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1398_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1398_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1398_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1398_Lane2" name="Sales Rep">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1398_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1398_Lane3" name="Loyalty Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1398_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1398_Lane4" name="Senior Data Scientist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1398_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1398_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1398_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1398_Start6" name="Scheduled — monthly model scoring run; quarterly model performance review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1398_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1398_Task7" name="Monthly scoring run">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly scoring run: system executes churn prediction model against all active trade/corporate accounts: (a) model inputs: purchase frequency (transactions/month), purchase volume trend (3-month rolling average vs. 12-month average), average transaction value trend, category breadth (number of departments purchased from), days since last purchase, payment behavior (average days to pay, bounced checks per W1381), customer service interactions (complaints per W41, W13.1), competitive proximity (distance to nearest competitor store), account tenure, seasonal purchasing pattern; (b) model output: churn probability score (0–100%) for each account; (c) risk classification: High Risk (&gt; 70% churn probability), Medium Risk (40–70%), Low Risk (&lt; 40%)
Responsible (R): System / Data Scientist
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: Automated (2–4 hours compute)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1398_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1398_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1398_Task8" name="At-risk account reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: At-risk account reporting: system generates monthly churn risk report for Head of Trade / Account Management and Credit Manager: (a) High Risk accounts with key contributing factors (e.g., &quot;purchase frequency declined 40% over 3 months&quot;, &quot;no purchases in 45 days despite typical weekly purchasing&quot;); (b) risk distribution: total revenue at risk by risk tier; (c) historical churn rate vs. predicted (model accuracy tracking); (d) recommended retention actions by risk tier
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1398_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1398_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1398_Task9" name="Retention action — Trade accounts">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Retention action — Trade accounts: Head of Trade / Account Management assigns High Risk trade accounts to Sales Reps for proactive outreach: (a) Sales Rep contacts customer within 5 business days: understand reason for reduced purchasing (competitor offering better price/terms? customer project completed? customer dissatisfied with service?); (b) for price-sensitive customers: offer price match or volume discount per W922; (c) for service complaints: escalate to Store Manager or Operations for resolution; (d) for project customers between projects: maintain relationship through contractor events (VS-12.3) and promotional offers; (e) Sales Rep logs outreach outcome in CRM
Responsible (R): Sales Rep / Head of Trade / Account Management
Accountable (A): VP Commercial
Duration: 20–30 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1398_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1398_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1398_Task10" name="Retention action — Loyalty members">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Retention action — Loyalty members: Loyalty Manager receives quarterly list of High Risk loyalty members: (a) design targeted retention campaign: personalized SMS/email with exclusive offer (double-points weekend, member-only discount coupon, early access to sale); (b) segment by churn driver: inactive members (no purchase in 60 days) vs. declining members (reduced frequency); (c) measure campaign effectiveness: reactivation rate (% of High Risk members who make a purchase within 30 days of campaign)
Responsible (R): Loyalty Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: Campaign-dependent</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1398_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1398_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1398_Task11" name="Quarterly model performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly model performance review: Senior Data Scientist evaluates model performance: (a) accuracy metrics: precision (what % of predicted churns actually churned?), recall (what % of actual churns did the model predict?), AUC-ROC curve; (b) feature importance: which factors are most predictive of churn?; (c) compare predicted vs. actual churn rate by risk tier; (d) if model performance degraded (AUC &lt; 0.75 or precision &lt; 60%), retrain model with updated data
Responsible (R): Senior Data Scientist
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1398_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1398_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1398_Task12" name="Annual model enhancement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual model enhancement: Senior Data Scientist evaluates new features and model improvements: (a) incorporate external data (construction industry index, regional building permit data as leading indicators); (b) test alternative algorithms (gradient boosting, neural networks vs. current logistic regression); (c) A/B test retention campaign effectiveness with and without model predictions; (d) present model ROI to BI Manager and VP Commercial: revenue retained through proactive outreach vs. cost of model development and retention campaigns
Responsible (R): Senior Data Scientist
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 20–30 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1398_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1398_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1398_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1398_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1398_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-327 (ensure controlled execution — Advanced Analytics (PA-28.3).) | - operational: Senior Data Scientist review and approval gate
Owner: Senior Data Scientist</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
