    <bpmn:process id="W_W1399" name="W1399. Store-Level Sales Forecasting Accuracy Monitoring, Model Drift Detection &amp; Retraining Trigger" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — monthly accuracy review; automated drift detection alerts
Frequency: Monthly accuracy monitoring; quarterly model drift assessment; retraining as triggered
Volume: 200 stores × 13 departments (~40 categories) = ~2,600 store-department forecasting units (up to ~8,000 at category grain) monitored monthly
Owner: Senior Data Scientist
Participants: Senior Data Scientist, BI Manager, Demand Planning Manager, VP Supply Chain
Source: workflow W1399 — Store-Level Sales Forecasting Accuracy Monitoring, Model Drift Detection &amp; Retraining Trigger</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1399_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1399_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1399_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1399_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1399_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1399_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1399_Lane2" name="Senior Data Scientist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1399_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1399_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1399_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1399_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1399_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1399_Start4" name="Scheduled — monthly accuracy review; automated drift detection alerts">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1399_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1399_Task5" name="Monthly accuracy computation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly accuracy computation: system automatically computes forecast accuracy metrics for each store-department for the prior month: (a) MAPE (Mean Absolute Percentage Error): absolute(actual − forecast) ÷ actual × 100%; (b) WAPE (Weighted Absolute Percentage Error): weighted by revenue contribution; (c) Bias: systematic over-forecasting (positive bias) vs. under-forecasting (negative bias); (d) compute at store level, department level, and chain level
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1399_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1399_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1399_Task6" name="Accuracy dashboard refresh">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Accuracy dashboard refresh: system updates forecasting accuracy dashboard: (a) chain-level MAPE and WAPE trend (rolling 12 months); (b) store-level accuracy heatmap (green: MAPE &lt; 15%, yellow: 15–25%, red: &gt; 25%); (c) department-level accuracy ranking (which departments are hardest to forecast?); (d) bias detection: stores/departments with consistent over- or under-forecasting; (e) accuracy vs. target (target MAPE: &lt; 15% at department level, &lt; 10% at store level)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1399_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1399_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1399_Task7" name="Drift detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Drift detection (monthly): system runs automated drift detection tests: (a) Data drift: have the statistical properties of input features changed? (e.g., average transaction value shifted, promotional frequency changed, day-of-week purchasing pattern shifted); (b) Concept drift: has the relationship between features and sales changed? (e.g., payday weekend effect weakened as digital payments spread); (c) Performance drift: has forecast accuracy degraded beyond threshold? (MAPE increased &gt; 5 percentage points from rolling 6-month average for 2+ consecutive months); if drift detected: system generates alert for Senior Data Scientist
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1399_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1399_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1399_Task8" name="Monthly accuracy review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly accuracy review: Senior Data Scientist and Demand Planning Manager review: (a) which stores/departments have MAPE &gt; 25% (red zone)?; (b) what are the root causes of large forecast errors? — new competitor opened near store? promotional event not captured in model? one-time event (local fiesta, typhoon closure)? supply-driven stockout (model forecasted demand but store was out of stock, so actual sales understated true demand)?; (c) identify stores/departments requiring manual forecast override for next month
Responsible (R): Senior Data Scientist / Demand Planning Mgr
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1399_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1399_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1399_Task9" name="Retraining trigger evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Retraining trigger evaluation: Senior Data Scientist evaluates whether drift detection alerts warrant model retraining: (a) Retrain if: performance drift confirmed at &gt; 3 stores or &gt; 2 departments chain-wide, or concept drift detected in key features, or seasonal pattern change detected (e.g., El Niño/La Niña shifting purchasing timing); (b) No retrain if: accuracy degradation is localized to 1–2 stores (local event), or within normal seasonal variation, or supply-driven (not forecast error); (c) if retrain: schedule retraining window (typically 1–2 weeks for data preparation, feature engineering, model training, validation, and deployment)
Responsible (R): Senior Data Scientist
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1399_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1399_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1399_Task10" name="Model retraining and deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Model retraining and deployment (when triggered): (a) Senior Data Scientist prepares updated training dataset: include latest 12 months of data, remove obsolete features, engineer new features based on drift analysis; (b) train updated model on historical data; (c) validate on holdout period (last 3 months): compare new model accuracy vs. current model; (d) if new model outperforms: deploy to production; if not: investigate further and try alternative approaches; (e) A/B test: run old and new models in parallel for 1 month to validate improvement in live environment; (f) document model version, training data range, features used, and validation results in model registry
Responsible (R): Senior Data Scientist
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 20–40 hours/retraining</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1399_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1399_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1399_Task11" name="Quarterly report to VP Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Quarterly report to VP Supply Chain: Senior Data Scientist presents quarterly forecasting accuracy summary: (a) chain-level MAPE trend, (b) inventory impact of forecast accuracy (estimated excess inventory cost from over-forecasting, estimated lost sales from under-forecasting), (c) model improvements made, (d) planned enhancements for next quarter
Responsible (R): Senior Data Scientist
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1399_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1399_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1399_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1399_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1399_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-327 (ensure controlled execution — Advanced Analytics (PA-28.3).) | - operational: Senior Data Scientist review and approval gate
Owner: Senior Data Scientist</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1399_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1399_Annotation13" targetRef="W1399_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
